# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository, and check it out as LF on every platform.
#
# Git for Windows defaults `core.autocrlf` on. A CRLF checkout gives .githooks/ a shebang ending in
# a carriage return, so the kernel looks for `bash\r`, every hook exits 127, and Git rejects the
# commit. It also loses `cargo fmt --check`, since rustfmt writes LF. `eol=lf` is the operative
# part - `text=auto` alone still yields CRLF worktrees there. Binary content is auto-detected and
# left untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
